> I'm thinking that we could make Simula a primitive language on inference? is it possible to hard-code it's input and processing as a stored-procedure kind of tool in inference? could we even make it so that the model can create it's own stored procedures using Simula and call them with information as gathered by the inference pass? is that realistic? powerful?

& [InterpretationBoundary] is non-authoritative
  + the candidate is a Simula-derived semantic process procedure surface callable by a model through governed tool turns
  + model proposal, deterministic compilation, admission, storage, and invocation remain distinct candidate operations
  + no generated procedure receives signature, effect, persistence, provider, or execution authority from model authorship alone
